invariant: INV-66
file: test/p256_adx_model.h
catches: diff_p256_adx
reason: model_round adds the high word of u times p's top word at word
  k + 4 without the carry the round before left, so the model is short by
  that bit in about one round in four. The model is what the assembly is
  held to, word for word. bin/diff_p256_adx holds the model to
  spec/lean/Spec/P256Adx.lean's reduce, whose proofs reduce_lt and
  reduce_mod are what make the Lean bounds a proof about this C.

--- old
                                (uint64_t)(multiple >> 64) + top};
--- new
                                (uint64_t)(multiple >> 64) + (top & 0U)};
